  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing (NAICS 339112) has seen $907M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The federal buying community issued 9,779 awards for this NAICS code, with an average award size of $92.8K. Obligations fell 43.7% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer, obligating $771M so far, while the Department of Defense obligated $61.8M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $53.9M. Contracting activity in prior full fiscal years ranged from $1.1B to $2.3B, with FY21 at $2.3B, FY22 at $1.1B, FY23 at $1.5B, FY24 at $2B, and FY25 at $1.6B. SDV OFFICE SYSTEMS LLC is the top vendor in FY2026 to date at $148M, followed by FIRST NATION GROUP LLC at $98M and OLYMPUS AMERICA INC at $83.7M. MEDICAL PLACE INC, MEDLINE INDUSTRIES, LP, and other suppliers also appear on the top 10 vendors list, reflecting concentrated buying and a small set of large contractors supplying federal customers.",
